# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values.
# `.env` is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit .env, then:
#   set -a; source .env; set +a

# Azure OpenAI - used by the detection / synthesis pipeline
# (src/core/llm_client.py).
#
# Comma-separated list of Azure OpenAI endpoint URLs. The client
# round-robins detection / synthesis calls across the pool, which
# raises effective TPM. Auth uses AzureCliCredential (run `az login`).
#
# Format: each entry is a full endpoint URL, e.g.
#   https://<resource>.openai.azure.com/
#
# Example (two endpoints):
#   AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINTS=https://aoai-east.openai.azure.com/,https://aoai-west.openai.azure.com/
#
# If unset, llm_client falls back to its built-in default pool.
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINTS=

# Microsoft Foundry Agents Service - used by the web-grounded
# verifier (src/verifier/agent_backend.py).
#
# DEFAULTS (no .env required): the verifier ships with a built-in
# round-robin pool of (endpoint, agent_id) pairs in
# ``DEFAULT_AGENT_ENDPOINTS`` / ``DEFAULT_AGENT_IDS`` (see
# src/verifier/agent_backend.py). Out-of-the-box behaviour is
# multi-endpoint round-robin across that pool. You only need to
# set anything below if you want to OVERRIDE the defaults (e.g.
# point at a private project, or pin to a single endpoint for
# debugging).
#
# Single-endpoint override (legacy):
#   AZURE_AGENTS_ENDPOINT - one project endpoint URL, shaped like
#     https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>
#   AZURE_AGENTS_VERIFIER_AGENT_ID - agent id (asst_...) with the
#     Web Search tool attached.
#
# Multi-endpoint override (round-robin across N projects):
#   AZURE_AGENTS_ENDPOINTS - comma-separated list of project
#     endpoint URLs.
#   AZURE_AGENTS_VERIFIER_AGENT_IDS - comma-separated list of
#     agent ids, paired POSITIONALLY with AZURE_AGENTS_ENDPOINTS.
#
# When both the singular and plural variants are set, the plurals
# win. The verifier's WebCache is shared across endpoints so a hit
# from any backend short-circuits the call.
#
# Auth uses AzureCliCredential, so run `az login` once - no API key
# is stored locally. The agent's model + system prompt are managed
# in the Foundry portal (we override `instructions` per run with
# prompts/verify_entity.yaml).

# --- Single-endpoint override (uncomment to use) ---
# AZURE_AGENTS_ENDPOINT=
# AZURE_AGENTS_VERIFIER_AGENT_ID=

# --- Multi-endpoint override (uncomment to use) ---
# AZURE_AGENTS_ENDPOINTS=https://a.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/p1,https://b.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/p2
# AZURE_AGENTS_VERIFIER_AGENT_IDS=asst_xxx,asst_yyy
